// Skill cape equip gates.
//
// The level check passes the ALREADY-EVALUATED stat as an int rather than taking a 'stat'
// parameter. 'stat' is a real type in engine.rs2 command signatures, but no script in this repo
// passes one as a proc/label argument, so it is unproven here - whereas stat_base(attack) as an
// int argument is ordinary and cannot surprise the compiler.
//
// Hoods are cosmetic and ungated, matching the live game.

[label,skillcape_require](int $level, string $skill, int $slot)
if ($level < 99) {
    mes("You need level 99 <$skill> to wear this cape.");
    return;
}
~equip($slot);

// Hunter's cape is imported but cannot be worn. As of 2026-09-22 Hunter IS a stat - it levels,
// saves and shows on the stats tab - but nothing in the world trains it and no Hunter emote has
// been converted out of the OSRS cache, so the cape stays shut off until the skill has content.
//
// Turning it on is four edits and they belong together: skillcape_cape, skillcape_cape_t and
// skillcape_hood gain a hunter row, skillcape_emotes.seq/.spotanim gain a converted emote, and
// these two lines become ~skillcape_require(stat_base(hunter), "Hunter", last_slot). The Max cape
// then counts 23 on its own - ~skillcape_stats reads skillcape_cape, not the stats enum, exactly
// so that this stays one decision in one place.
[label,skillcape_unavailable](string $what)
mes("<$what> is not available on this server yet, so this cape cannot be worn.");

// THE MAX CAPE: level 99 in every skill that HAS a cape - ~skillcape_stats, 22 of them, and see the
// note on that proc in skillcape_shop.rs2 for why it is no longer the stats enum outright. The gate
// is still a count rather than a list of names, and still follows the data on its own.
[opheld2,max_cape]
if (~skillcape_count_99s < ~skillcape_stats) {
    mes("You need level 99 in all <tostring(~skillcape_stats)> skills to wear the Max cape.");
    return;
}
~equip(last_slot);

[opheld2,attack_cape] @skillcape_require(stat_base(attack), "Attack", last_slot);
[opheld2,attack_cape_t] @skillcape_require(stat_base(attack), "Attack", last_slot);
